  "snapshot": "freecad-path0.21.2",
  "instruction": "Start with /home/user/Desktop/part.step and /home/user/Desktop/fixture.step in FreeCAD Path/CAM 0.21.2. To use FreeCAD, run `freecad` from a terminal (use the full executable path if it is not on PATH). For this task, use `/usr/lib/freecad/bin/freecadcmd-python3` for FreeCAD Path command-line automation when working on `part.step`.\n\nThe part is a 120 x 80 x 18 mm blank. Create one G54 Path Job from the part and machine a centered 50 x 30 mm top Pocket Shape from Z18 to a final floor at Z13 with 2.5 mm step-downs; a D10 cutter naturally leaves R5 internal corners. Use T1 as a D10 flat end mill with a 10 mm shank, at S7000 rpm and horizontal/vertical feed F500 mm/min. Link the imported fixture as the operation's check-geometry reference and set fixture clearance to 3 mm. Because FreeCAD 0.21.2 Pocket Shape has no native arbitrary-solid check-geometry property, apply a native Boundary Dressup as the active Job operation, outside an exclusion envelope made by offsetting the fixture by the 5 mm cutter radius plus the 3 mm clearance; retain editable links from the Pocket Shape, envelope, and dressup to the imported fixture. Use Safe Height Z26 and Clearance Height Z27. Every complete cutter swept envelope, including line and arc interiors, must remain at least 3 mm from the fixture. Use the LinuxCNC postprocessor and save the editable document and posted program exactly as /home/user/Desktop/task-10.FCStd and /home/user/Desktop/task-10.nc.",
